ong Boise’s cultural pioneers. She arrived in Boise in 1884 with her husband, irrigation engineer Arthur Foote. The city will celebrate Hallock Foote’s life and contributions with a day of activities at Boise Public Library’s main branch, 715 S. Capitol Blvd., on Saturday, June 11, from 10 a.m. to 4 p.m."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},"smart_blocks:2016-06-06 - Boise honors artist, pioneer, social critic Mary Hallock Foote.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"zt8hwl","at":1785795008446},"key":"2016-06-06 - Boise honors artist, pioneer, social critic Mary Hallock Foote.md#---frontmatter---","lines":[1,9],"size":633,"outlinks":[{"title":"By Anna Webb","target":"By Anna Webb","line":5}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
